<title>USA: &quot;Empire Strikes Back,&quot; &quot;Star Wars&quot; top box office.</title>
<headline>&quot;Empire Strikes Back,&quot; &quot;Star Wars&quot; top box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the Feb. 21-23 weekend box office, Exhibitor Relations Co. said Monday.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. The Empire</p>
<p>    Strikes Back	    $21,975,993	 $ ----</p>
<p>2. Star Wars		  $11,031,743	 $115,952,747</p>
<p>3. Absolute Power	   $ 9,014,333	 $ 28,700,130</p>
<p>4. Dante's Peak	     $ 7,137,185	 $ 45,453,535</p>
<p>5. Vegas Vacation	   $ 6,549,243	 $ 21,279,992</p>
<p>6. Fools Rush In	    $ 5,511,620	 $ 16,557,808</p>
<p>7. That Darn Cat	    $ 3,625,278	 $ 11,178,789</p>
<p>8. Rosewood		   $ 3,154,075	 $  ----</p>
<p>9. Jerry Maguire	    $ 3,080,444	 $131,653,945</p>
<p>10 The English Patient    $ 2,823,228	 $ 51,532,324</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; and &quot;Star Wars&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Absolute Power,&quot; &quot;Fools Rush In&quot; and &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; are released by Sony Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;Dante's Peak&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Vegas Vacation&quot; and &quot;Rosewood&quot; are released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;That Darn Cat&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;The English Patient&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Disney.</p>
</text>
